# FORMAT-03 NIE golden manifest.
#
# Each line selects one vendored NIE fixture and records its reported
# dimensions, its wire pixel encoding, and the canonical CRC-32 (IEEE) of the
# width*height*4 premultiplied image.RGBA Pix bytes that the host writes into
# the caller's image.RGBA Pix (guest RGBA_PREMUL + host row copy).
#
# The expected pixels are independently derived from the NIE wire format per
# ../wuffs/doc/spec/nie-spec.md and the Wuffs v0.4 pixel-swizzler arithmetic
# (wuffs-mirror-release-c/release/c/wuffs-v0.4.c): bn4 applies
# color_u32_argb_nonpremul__as__color_u32_argb_premul's a*0x101*0x101
# arithmetic, bn8 applies color_u64_argb_nonpremul__as__color_u32_argb_premul,
# bp4 copies the premultiplied bytes, and bp8 takes each channel's high byte
# via color_u64__as__color_u32 (NIE is little-endian BGRA, 4 or 8 bytes per
# pixel). The animated-red-blue.nia value covers frame zero only (the 8-byte
# CDD and inner NIE header are skipped; later frames are untouched).
# None of the values were obtained from this package's wasm decoder;
# decode_nie_integration_test.go reproduces the full derivation bit-for-bit
# and asserts the per-pixel bytes, not just these CRCs.
#
# The four 49 encoding variants (bn4, bn8, bp4, bp8) encode the same 16x16
# image: bn8/bp4/bp8 decode to byte-identical premultiplied RGBA (the
# conversion round-trips exactly) while bn4's 8-bit non-premultiplied
# quantisation differs in 63 of 256 pixels. That is expected; each variant
# still exercises its own 4- or 8-bytes-per-pixel wire path and its own
# premul semantics.
#
# Columns: file width height pixel_encoding premul_rgba_crc32
49.bn4.nie 16 16 bn4 1884754942
49.bn8.nie 16 16 bn8 787867622
49.bp4.nie 16 16 bp4 787867622
49.bp8.nie 16 16 bp8 787867622
crude-flag.nie 3 2 bn4 2359083796
hippopotamus.nie 36 28 bn4 3183889069
animated-red-blue.nia 64 48 nia-bn4 4230696731
